The Glasgow subway first opened in 1896 as a cable -hauled system.

127
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:55,360
It is generally recognized as the world's underground railway after London and

128
00:10:55,360 --> 00:11:01,500
Budapest. In its long history it has never been expanded, remaining as a single loop

129
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,140
line with a mere 15 stations.

130
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:09,760
At its peak it served the shipyard workers on the south side of the city.

131
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:16,480
In the 1960s there was a decline in the shipbuilding industry and the popularity of

132
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,080
private transport grew.

133
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:23,140
As a result, the subway saw a rapid decline in ridership.

134
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:30,860
It ran with little further change until 1977 when its new operators closed it for

135
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:32,900
major modernization investment.

136
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:39,720
Carriages were replaced, ventilation was improved, and the main depot was also

137
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:45,120
renovated and fitted with connecting tracks to replace the outdated crane transfer

138
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:52,740
mechanism. The subway in its present form reopened for operation in April 1980.

139
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:57,980
Since its relaunch, the subway has seen a revival in its fortunes.

140
00:11:57,980 --> 00:12:04,160
It serves as a viable alternative to other forms of transport and has gone a long

141
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:07,220
way to alleviate traffic jams in the city center.

142
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:13,760
In 1996 the system reached an important milestone, 100 years.

143
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:18,780
To commemorate this special event, the color scheme of the train carriages was

144
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:25,880
updated. Recently, high -tech systems such as smart card ticketing machines and

145
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:29,460
smart gates are used across all subway stations.

146
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:35,840
The smart card provides more convenient travel and passengers simply top up their

147
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:38,980
cards and tap them to get in and out the subway.

148
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:45,340
Since its launch, the technology has been adopted by more than 100,000 subway

149
